      "id": "bb84e997-1451-4006-bf69-4784eded0786",
      "name": "Phase One Final Research",
      "description": "This four-week research assignment investigates one of the fundamental challenges in modern Generative AI: how to develop more capable AI systems while significantly reducing the amount of training data and computational resources required.\nRecent breakthroughs in Generative AI have primarily been achieved through scaling model size, increasing dataset volume, and utilizing massive computational infrastructure. While this approach has demonstrated exceptional performance, it is expensive, difficult to reproduce, and inaccessible to many researchers and organizations.\nThis research assignment challenges participants to explore an alternative direction: improving the efficiency of learning rather than relying on larger models or larger datasets.\nThe objective is to conduct original research into methodologies that enable Generative AI systems to achieve competitive performance with substantially less data, lower computational requirements, and shorter training times.\n",
