      "name": "Understanding LLMs",
      "description": "This content introduces the fundamentals of Large Language Models (LLMs), the AI systems that power modern generative AI applications such as chatbots, coding assistants, and content generation tools. Participants will explore how LLMs are built, the concepts of tokens, embeddings, transformers, pre-training, and fine-tuning, and how these models produce human-like responses. The lesson also examines practical use cases, common challenges such as hallucinations and bias, and best practices for using LLMs effectively and responsibly as a foundation for developing AI-powered applications.",
